it was immediately obvious that the  attack on a russian air base in crimea  was a big one  thick clouds of smoke could be seen from  miles away and the explosions sent  russian tourists heading for cover  i went out to look at the window and it  was as if a mushroom cloud from a  nuclear explosion had risen there there  were two big explosions like that  everything began to fall around and  collapse crimea is deep in russian  occupied territory the kremlin has been  using the air base to launch attacks on  ukraine  russia said the explosions were just an  accident on the base and the ukrainians  are yet to officially acknowledge their  involvement but a senior official here  has told us that it was ukrainian  special forces who carried out the  attack  it is a big coup for kiev and it will be  deeply uncomfortable for moscow  the russian side must be feeling quite  nervous at this point that they're not  making good progress that ukraine keeps  fighting as effectively as they do and  striking back against an important air  base and doing so in an area in form of  crimea that's so important to russia  crimea was illegally annexed by russia  in 2014.  the saki air base that was attacked  yesterday is on the peninsula's west  coast more than 150 miles behind russian  front lines  satellite imagery taken yesterday before  the attacks shows at least 30 russian  aircraft on the tarmac ukrainian sources  say that nine fighter jets were  destroyed and others damaged  one person was killed  we cannot verify precise figures though  only one out of the 14 injured are  hospitalized the rest are at home thank  god they all have light injuries the  main task now is the repair of  infrastructure we have 62 multi-story  buildings damaged  overnight russian forces hit back  shelling apartment blocks a school and a  concert hall in the dinipro region at  least 13 civilians were killed  today videos posted on social media  showed long queues of cars trying to  leave crimea the reality of a brutal war  that most russians have been shielded  from came too close to home alistair  bunker sky news in ukraine
 

